# SpendScope

Next.js 15 (App Router, JS/JSX) + React 19 + Redux Toolkit + Tailwind v4. Local-first (IndexedDB)
with optional Supabase sync; web companion of the Android/iOS apps (Android source in `../spend_scope_android`).

**Before working on anything, read `docs/README.md`**, then the doc for the area you touch:
`docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`, `docs/DATA_AND_SYNC.md`, `docs/FEATURES.md`, `docs/CALCULATORS.md`,
`docs/DESIGN_SYSTEM.md`, `docs/SECURITY_AND_PRIVACY.md`, `docs/DEVELOPMENT.md`,
`docs/HISTORY_AND_DECISIONS.md`.

## Non-negotiable rules

- Never modify `../spend_scope_android`. Never mutate the remote Supabase project without explicit approval.
- Data flow: UI → hooks (`src/hooks`) → services (`src/services`) → `src/lib/localDb.js` (IndexedDB + sync outbox).
  Components must not call Supabase or IndexedDB directly.
- The Supabase DB is shared with the Android/iOS apps and owned by the mobile team: never alter it from here;
  all cloud column knowledge lives in `src/lib/remoteSchema.js`; deletes are soft deletes (see `docs/DATA_AND_SYNC.md` §3).
- Money: aggregate in integer minor units (`Math.round(x*100)`); format with `formatMoney`. Zero-decimal: JPY/KRW/VND.
- Account transfers are paired rows with `transfer_group_id` and must be excluded from income/expense totals.
- Dates use `src/lib/dateUtils.js` (local midnight → UTC ISO); remotely the date is `transactions.created_at`.
- App Lock/PIN data is device-local and never synced. Seed defaults only after a successful pull.
- Use CSS variable tokens (`var(--home-*)`); theme changes go through Redux, not the `dark` class.
- Add/adjust tests for calculation, sync or money changes. Definition of done: `npm run lint` (0 warnings),
  `npm test`, `npm run build`, relevant Playwright spec.
- Update the matching file in `docs/` whenever behavior, schema, routes or conventions change.
